; Comments here start with a semicolon. Windows' profile API does not treat `#`
; as a comment marker, so a `#key=value` line reaches the component as a key
; literally named `#key` rather than as a disabled setting.

[wambridge]
device=M5
volume=4

; Milliseconds of silence prepended to the stream, 0..10000, default 1500.
; This is straight added delay on a path about 6 s long, and it is the only part
; of that delay the project adds to itself. It has been there since the initial
; import with no comment explaining why. Measured at 0 on hardware 2026-08-08:
; startup still reaches WAMBRIDGE PLAYING, so that is 1.5 s back.
;startup_silence=0

; Speaker-facing format: flac, wav or mp3, default flac. Thinner is not faster -
; mp3 at 320 kbps measured worse than flac, 16.9 s against 13.4 s, because a
; prebuffer bounded by bytes holds more seconds of a thinner stream. wav pulls
; the same lever the other way: measured 5.68 s against flac's 6.67 s over the
; same source, with half the variation, because its bitrate does not ride the
; music. The cost is depth - flac carries 24 bit here and wav is fixed at 16, and
; its transport passed the checklist on instruments with nobody listening, so it
; stays opt-in. flac is the default and this line only shows the syntax.
;format=flac

; Milliseconds of queue kept on top of foobar's own buffer length, 0..10000,
; default 2000. Capacity is delay here almost one for one: the queue was measured
; running 3.79-3.99 s full of its 4.0 s capacity, which makes this the largest
; single share of the delay and the one nobody ever measured. Lower it to find
; where the pipe starves - starving shows as free climbing in the CLOCK line and
; as audible dropouts, not as a better number.
;buffer_extra=1000

; Seconds of sleep timer armed once a stream ends, 0..86400, default 0 (off).
; This firmware has no idle power-down at all - GetPowerSaving and
; GetAutoPowerDown do not exist - so stopping playback leaves the M5 lit until
; something asks it to sleep, and SetSleepTimer is the only thing it answers.
; The timer clears itself once it fires and is cleared again when the next
; stream starts, so nothing stays configured on the speaker. Off by default,
; because powering the speaker down is not this component's decision to make.
;sleep_after_stop=120

; Per-second CLOCK line in the foobar console. Diagnostic only; caps itself at
; 240 lines. Turn it on before reporting anything about pacing.
;diagnostics=1
